From: SM-X710 bring-up <gts9wifi@example.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dpu: start the command-mode engine when the encoder is enabled

A command-mode (DSI) panel receives nothing until the CTL path has been flushed
and started, and that kickoff is issued from the atomic flush of the commit that
enables the CRTC.  The DRM atomic commit order is disable -> planes -> enable,
so that flush runs *before* dpu_crtc_enable() has enabled the physical encoder:
_dpu_encoder_kickoff_phys() skips encoders whose enable_state is still
DPU_ENC_DISABLED, and the flush and start are lost.  dpu_encoder_phys_cmd_enable()
programs the interface but never starts it either, so the first frame of every
enable is never scanned out.

On a system with a compositor this is invisible: the compositor's next page flip
commits again and kicks the engine, and the frame after that is fine.  On a
fbcon-only system (no composer, no page flips) there is no next commit - fbcon
writes directly into the scanout buffer - and the panel never receives a single
frame.  What the user sees is the DDIC's power-on RAM at brightness, and then the
DDIC blanking itself after its no-data timeout.

Measured on the SM-X710 with the AMSA10FA01 panel: every unblank logged

  [drm:dpu_encoder_helper_wait_for_irq] *ERROR* encoder is disabled id=35,
      callback=dpu_encoder_phys_cmd_ctl_start_irq, IRQ=[1, 9]

from dpu_encoder_phys_cmd_wait_for_commit_done() -> _dpu_encoder_phys_cmd_wait_for_ctl_start()
(is_started() false because the CTL was never started), and dmesg showed panel id
80 00 04 with a valid plane/crtc state while the panel never changed content.

Flush and start at the end of the encoder enable, next to the register
programming that has just made the interface ready.
---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder_phys_cmd.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder_phys_cmd.c
index 45079ee59..ab34c7003 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder_phys_cmd.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder_phys_cmd.c
@@ -486,6 +486,22 @@ static void dpu_encoder_phys_cmd_enable(struct dpu_encoder_phys *phys_enc)
 
 	dpu_encoder_phys_cmd_enable_helper(phys_enc);
 	phys_enc->enable_state = DPU_ENC_ENABLED;
+
+	/*
+	 * A command-mode panel only shows something once the CTL path has been
+	 * flushed and started, and that normally happens in the atomic flush of
+	 * this very commit - which runs *before* the CRTC is enabled.  The
+	 * kickoff there skips physical encoders that are still disabled, so the
+	 * first frame after every enable is never started.  Nothing else starts
+	 * it either: fbcon writes straight into the scanout buffer without
+	 * committing, so on a compositor-less system the panel keeps showing
+	 * its power-on RAM until it blanks itself.  Flush and start here.
+	 */
+	if (phys_enc->hw_ctl->ops.trigger_flush) {
+		dpu_encoder_phys_inc_pending(phys_enc);
+		phys_enc->hw_ctl->ops.trigger_flush(phys_enc->hw_ctl);
+	}
+	dpu_encoder_helper_trigger_start(phys_enc);
 }
 
 static void _dpu_encoder_phys_cmd_connect_te(
